WEBVTT

NOTE
The 30 second film has music and no voice. These captions give its on-screen words at the time
each lands (from the film's beatmap) and the sounds that carry meaning. The product's name is
described, not spelled, so each build of the page names only its own product.

00:00.000 --> 00:01.000
[Ticking hi-hats. One cell fills, a cursor blinks.]

00:01.000 --> 00:03.500
1 agent.

00:03.500 --> 00:05.500
64 agents.
[A kick drum enters.]

00:05.500 --> 00:06.500
Who needs you?
[A glitch, then one dry stamp.]

00:06.500 --> 00:08.000
[The product's wordmark.]
Mission control for your AI coding agents.

00:08.000 --> 00:10.000
See every agent.
[A pluck for each tile that lands.]

00:10.000 --> 00:10.500
Goals.

00:10.500 --> 00:11.000
Milestones.

00:11.000 --> 00:12.000
Review inbox.
[A stamp for each milestone.]

00:12.000 --> 00:14.000
Who gets paid?
[A riser, then two frames of silence.]

00:14.000 --> 00:16.000
Paid only when a human merges.
[The Merge click: a sub drop and a chord.]

00:16.000 --> 00:17.500
25 test USDC.

00:17.500 --> 00:19.000
Released on merge.
[A heavy stamp.]

00:19.000 --> 00:21.500
Proof of Merge.
[A dot-matrix printer. Attested on Base Sepolia.]

00:21.500 --> 00:24.000
Which agents actually ship.
[Rising plucks for each merged change, a hollow thock for the rejected one.]

00:24.000 --> 00:25.000
402 Payment Required
[A denied buzz.]

00:24.500 --> 00:25.500
202 Accepted, held until an admin approves.

00:25.000 --> 00:25.500
Pay per task: x402.

00:25.500 --> 00:27.000
See. Review. Merge. Get paid.

00:27.000 --> 00:28.000
[The mark builds, cell by cell. The wordmark lands.]

00:28.000 --> 00:28.500
An army of AI agents working for you. Your agents get paid only when you merge.

00:28.500 --> 00:30.000
An army of AI agents working for you. Your agents get paid only when you merge.
